# 1. PLATFORM IDENTITY

OFFSLEEK is one unified school-management technology ecosystem consisting of five separate applications that operate on a common backend.

The five applications are not independent products. They are five different interfaces to the same school-management platform.

Each application has a specific responsibility, user group and set of permissions.

All five applications must follow one common architecture, data model, naming convention, identity system and integration standard.

### Core architectural principle

**One OFFSLEEK platform. Five applications. One shared backend. One consistent source of truth.**

The applications must remain separate projects. Do not merge their codebases into one application.

