# 3. SHARED BACKEND ARCHITECTURE

All five applications must use the same Firebase project.

### Existing Firebase project

Project ID: `offsleek-shared-backend`

Existing configuration:

- Firebase Authentication enabled with Email/Password.
- Cloud Firestore default database.
- Firestore region: `asia-south1`.
- Firebase modular SDK.
- Shared Firebase initialization using the singleton pattern.

The existing Firebase configuration must be preserved.

Every application must initialize Firebase using the existing project configuration and must not accidentally initialize a separate Firebase project.

### Architecture diagram

```text
                  OFFSLEEK PLATFORM
                          |
          ---------------------------------
          |               |               |
     Super Admin      Internal Staff    School OS
      Dashboard        Dashboard
          |               |               |
          --------------- | ---------------
                          |
                SHARED FIREBASE BACKEND
                          |
          ---------------------------------
          |               |               |
      Firestore      Firebase Auth    Cloud Storage
          |
     Shared School Data
          |
          -------------------------------
          |                             |
      Staff App                  Parent & Student App
          |                             |
          -------- Shared Records -------
```

Cloud Functions or another trusted server-side service may be introduced for sensitive operations, payment verification, privileged writes and notifications. These services must be implemented and deployed separately; do not assume they already exist.

### Important

Firebase configuration alone does not mean an application is integrated.

Each application must actually:
- Authenticate users.
- Read authorized records.
- Write permitted records.
- Listen for relevant updates.
- Handle errors and loading states.
- Enforce school-level data isolation.

