# 6. SCHOOL IDENTITY AND MULTI-TENANT ISOLATION

OFFSLEEK is a multi-school platform.

Each school is an independent tenant.

For example:

```text
OFFSLEEK
  |
  |-- School A
  |     |-- Students
  |     |-- Parents
  |     |-- Staff
  |     |-- Classes
  |     |-- Attendance
  |
  |-- School B
  |     |-- Students
  |     |-- Parents
  |     |-- Staff
  |     |-- Classes
  |     |-- Attendance
  |
  |-- School C
        |-- Students
        |-- Parents
        |-- Staff
        |-- Classes
        |-- Attendance
```

Every school-level read and write must be restricted to the authenticated user's authorized school.

A school ID supplied by a client must never be trusted on its own.

The backend must verify that the authenticated user is authorized to access that school.

Super Admin access across schools must be explicitly authorized.

Internal staff must only access the school information permitted by their department and assigned permissions.

Parents and students must not gain access to records by changing a school ID, student ID or document ID in the frontend.

