# 19. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

OFFSLEEK should not be declared fully integrated until these tests pass.

### School identity
- A school created in Internal Staff Dashboard appears in Super Admin Dashboard.
- School OS identifies the same school.
- All school records use the same school ID.

### Student identity
- A student created in School OS is accessible to authorized Staff App users.
- Parent App can access the student only through an explicit parent-student link.
- Student App can access the student's own permitted information.

### Attendance
- Attendance submitted in Staff App appears in School OS.
- Parent App displays the linked child's attendance.
- Student App displays the student's attendance.
- All portals reference the same attendance record.
- Changes and corrections follow the audit process.

### Data isolation
- School A cannot read School B's records.
- Parent A cannot read Parent B's child records.
- Student A cannot read Student B's records.
- Teacher A cannot access unassigned classes.
- Internal employees cannot exceed their assigned permissions.

### Reliability
- Data survives page refresh.
- Duplicate records are not created.
- Real-time listeners work where implemented.
- Offline or network errors are handled.
- Security rules prevent unauthorized reads and writes.
- Test data does not contaminate production data.

